# Live query-memory admission over row buffers and result collectors (memory.md §2-§5, Q1).
# A jed-specific resource contract, not a PostgreSQL limit. Each budget is the exact peak of
# logical row bytes (ROW 32 + Σ VALUE 32 + payload) the statement holds; the record below it at
# budget - 1 fails 54P05. Pre-projection relation rows count only their touched columns' payloads
# (memory.md §3), which keeps the thresholds identical in the memory and disk storage modes. The
# blocking-operator shapes whose lane differs between those modes live in query_memory_eager.test.
# requires: query.select, ddl.create_table, dml.insert, dml.insert_multi_row, dml.insert_select, dml.update, dml.delete, dml.returning, types.text, query.cross_join, query.comma_from, query.join_left, query.join_inner, query.lateral, query.set_returning, query.values, query.derived_table, query.union, query.intersect, query.cte, query.cte_recursive, query.window, query.window_ranking, query.subquery_scalar, query.subquery_exists, query.subquery_correlated, query.aggregates, query.order_by, query.limit, func.casing, query.explain, resource.cost_limit, resource.query_memory

